My classmates insult me for being gay, what can I do? Is being gay wrong?

I’m sorry to hear that you’re being insulted by your classmates. No one deserves to be treated that way. Being gay is not wrong at all. Everyone has the right to be who they are and to love who they love. It’s important to remember that you’re not alone. There are many people and organizations that support and advocate for the LGBTQ+ community. If you feel comfortable, you could talk to a trusted adult, such as a teacher or counselor, about what’s happening. They may be able to help you address the situation and provide support. It’s also important to take care of yourself. Surround yourself with supportive friends and family members, and engage in activities that make you feel happy and fulfilled. Remember that you are valuable and deserving of respect and kindness

